{"study_accession":"PRJNA1050781","secondary_study_accession":"SRP477172","title":"Dynamic molecular signatures of acute myocardial infarction based on transcriptomics","description":"Peripheral blood mononuclear cells were collected from the patients. RNA-seq and analysis was performed on the collected samples. Total RNA was extracted from the tissue using TRIzol® Reagent according the manufacturer’s instructions(Invitrogen) and genomic DNA was removed using DNase I (TaKara). Then RNA quality was determined using 2100 Bioanalyser (Agilent) and quantified using the ND-2000 (NanoDrop Technologies). High-quality RNA sample (OD260/280=1.8~2.2, OD260/230≥2.0, RIN≥6.5, 28S:18S≥1.0, >10μg) is used to construct sequencing library Overall design: We enrolled patients with AMI aged between 30 and 70. RNA-seq analysis was performed on the peripheral blood mononuclear cells collected from the patients at three time points: 1 day, 7 days, and 3 months after AMI. Differential genes and metabolites between groups were screened by bio-informatics methods to understand the dynamic changes of AMI in different periods.","pubmed":"38702356","geo_series":"","n_samples":15,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN38753431","study_accession":"PRJNA1050781","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"YJXQ5","description":"YJXQ5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7964841","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-05-10","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["tissue","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["cell_type","myocardial infarction"],["genotype","leukocyte"],["treatment","acute stage"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR27166017","experiment_accession":"SRX22846944","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":21795862,"base_count":6538758600,"first_public":"2024-05-10","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7